Add a libplacebo filter option, nv12_output, that selects the renderer's
direct NV12 output mode through pl_renderer_set_nv12_output(). With
nv12_output=match and format=nv12:range=tv, a VAAPI tone-mapping chain can
render straight into the reverse-mapped NV12 surface (patch 0023,
ETV_VAAPI_DIRECT_NV12=1) with the same output as format=rgba followed by
scale_vulkan=format=nv12:out_range=limited, in one pass.

The option exists only when FFmpeg is built against a libplacebo that
defines PL_RENDERER_NV12_OUTPUT (patches/libplacebo/0001, docker build
argument DIRECT_NV12_OUTPUT=1). Against a stock libplacebo it is not
compiled in, so `ffmpeg -h filter=libplacebo` lists it only when the
implementation is present. The mode is set per renderer, so other libplacebo
filters in the same process are unaffected. The default, off, keeps the
current behavior. Targets that do not qualify keep libplacebo's normal
output path.

diff --git a/libavfilter/vf_libplacebo.c b/libavfilter/vf_libplacebo.c
